                                   '\n'
                                   'Dining sets may include a dining table, individual dining chairs, and a matching '
                                   'bench.\n'
                                   '\n'
                                   'A dining table belonging to the identified dining set is product, not context.\n'
                                   '\n'
                                   'Sofa sets may include sofas, loveseats, and armchairs arranged together as one '
                                   'seating group.\n'
                                   '\n'
                                   'Armchairs that sit in the seating group are product even when their colour, '
                                   'fabric, pattern, or shape differs from the sofas; also list them in '
                                   'unclear_membership.\n'
                                   '\n'
                                   'An armchair placed apart from the seating group is context.\n'
                                   '\n'
                                   'In every set, coffee tables, side tables, consoles, sideboards, buffets, and '
                                   'shelving are context, even when they match the set, unless the photo is selling '
                                   'that piece on its own. List a matching one in unclear_membership.\n'
                                   '\n'
                                   'Any other furniture whose membership is uncertain: decide the role from the rules '
                                   'above and list it in unclear_membership.\n'
                                   '\n'
                                   'HOME TEXTILES\n'
                                   '\n'
                                   'For home textiles, the primary textile item is product.\n'
                                   '\n'
                                   'Examples include cushions, throws, bedding, curtains, and rugs when these are the '
